If you choose Oreo, it says, you're a bit of a piece of work.

1130
00:48:41.410 --> 00:48:43.170
From the outside, you're sweet.

1131
00:48:43.350 --> 00:48:44.370
I mean, who wouldn't be?

1132
00:48:44.510 --> 00:48:48.950
But once people dig deep enough, they'll find out you've got some very profound secrets.

1133
00:48:49.270 --> 00:48:50.450
Are any of these good?

1134
00:48:50.570 --> 00:48:50.970
Yeah.

1135
00:48:51.210 --> 00:48:52.910
Well, I'll tell you what.

1136
00:48:53.070 --> 00:48:53.710
I'll tell you what.

1137
00:48:53.710 --> 00:48:55.110
I'm going to end with this one because...

1138
00:48:55.690 --> 00:48:56.370
Is it lemon?

1139
00:48:56.510 --> 00:48:57.650
Because I also love lemon.

1140
00:48:57.850 --> 00:48:58.530
It's lemon!

1141
00:48:58.850 --> 00:49:00.070
Oh, that was the one.

1142
00:49:00.150 --> 00:49:02.170
I didn't say that one because I love lemon.

1143
00:49:02.170 --> 00:49:02.830
Oh, no.

1144
00:49:03.050 --> 00:49:03.730
Oh, no.

1145
00:49:03.730 --> 00:49:05.910
So, I almost picked lemon.

1146
00:49:06.150 --> 00:49:10.250
If the bakery where I got our cupcakes would have had lemon, I would have gotten lemon.

1147
00:49:10.270 --> 00:49:11.070
I love lemon.

1148
00:49:11.310 --> 00:49:14.370
But it didn't, so I had to go with the chocolate with vanilla frosting.

1149
00:49:14.390 --> 00:49:18.390
Yeah, vanilla's like, I'll take vanilla, but if there's lemon, I'll almost always pick it.

1150
00:49:18.470 --> 00:49:19.610
But there's usually not.

1151
00:49:19.930 --> 00:49:20.830
Okay, well.

1152
00:49:21.070 --> 00:49:21.450
Uh-oh.

1153
00:49:22.610 --> 00:49:28.590
Lemon is, quote, the one who hates 90% of the friend group but pretends to love all of them.

1154
00:49:30.900 --> 00:49:36.740
This is the take on cupcakes.

1155
00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:40.780
Someone was dumped by a cupcake or someone was broken up with by a cupcake.

1156
00:49:41.400 --> 00:49:42.380
Here's what it says.

1157
00:49:42.540 --> 00:49:47.200
If you're eating a lemon cupcake, it says, you've got an attitude no one can quite understand.

1158
00:49:48.540 --> 00:49:53.020
Everyone loves you, but you're a little bit less sweet and loving than everyone else is.

1159
00:49:53.140 --> 00:49:53.760
It's okay.

1160
00:49:54.260 --> 00:49:56.520
Sometimes it's hard to love crazy bitches.

1161
00:49:57.560 --> 00:49:58.040
Whoa!

1162
00:49:58.740 --> 00:49:59.820
So, what am I?

1163
00:49:59.960 --> 00:50:02.380
Am I unoriginal or am I a crazy bitch?

1164
00:50:02.560 --> 00:50:03.540
Maybe a little about...

1165
00:50:03.540 --> 00:50:04.020
I'm a, like...

1166
00:50:04.020 --> 00:50:04.720
A little column A?

1167
00:50:04.900 --> 00:50:05.680
A little column B.

1168
00:50:07.280 --> 00:50:08.480
Well, there you have it.

1169
00:50:08.620 --> 00:50:10.980
That's what your cupcake choice says about you.

1170
00:50:11.320 --> 00:50:14.360
Spoon University is a harsh place.

1171
00:50:15.580 --> 00:50:15.980
Damn.

1172
00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:17.940
Can I have my cupcake now?

1173
00:50:18.720 --> 00:50:19.120
Sure.

1174
00:50:20.320 --> 00:50:21.580
Dig in, everybody.

1175
00:50:23.060 --> 00:50:26.720
Well, lady, I will say, you and I both love lemon cupcakes, so what does that say?

1176
00:50:26.900 --> 00:50:28.780
I guess we're a couple of crazy bitches.

1177
00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:29.420
I guess so.

1178
00:50:30.440 --> 00:50:30.980
All right.

1179
00:50:31.080 --> 00:50:33.120
Well, now we're going to go back to Aunt Shirley's house.

1180
00:50:33.460 --> 00:50:36.540
Her family has gathered to watch a farewell video.

1181
00:50:37.200 --> 00:50:38.280
It's like her will?

1182
00:50:38.900 --> 00:50:39.300
Yes.

1183
00:50:39.700 --> 00:50:40.720
I wrote this.

1184
00:50:40.840 --> 00:50:45.760
I did not play a bullsh** card here, but I would like to say that this video lays a lot of pipe.

1185
00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:49.540
Well, we also had to reshoot this video.

1186
00:50:49.890 --> 00:50:52.000
We mentioned this during Moving On.

1187
00:50:52.280 --> 00:50:57.140
There was originally a different woman cast as Aunt Shirley in the pilot of the farm,

1188
00:50:57.140 --> 00:51:01.600
and this was the only thing that that actress had to do was just read this will.

1189
00:51:01.600 --> 00:51:08.680
But when they wrote Moving On and they expanded the role, they cast just legendary character

1190
00:51:08.680 --> 00:51:10.680
actress Mary Gillis in the role.

1191
00:51:10.920 --> 00:51:16.740
Well, this video sets up the whole entire series if it would have gone.

1192
00:51:16.960 --> 00:51:17.660
Listen to this.

1193
00:51:18.120 --> 00:51:19.540
Aunt Shirley on the video says,

1194
00:51:19.680 --> 00:51:21.360
Thank you for coming to my funeral.

1195
00:51:21.720 --> 00:51:25.940
As I gaze at life's big sunset, I can't help but wonder where it all went wrong.

1196
00:51:26.120 --> 00:51:27.980
You've all disappointed me greatly.

1197
00:51:28.320 --> 00:51:30.420
Fanny, a single mama in the city.

1198
00:51:30.900 --> 00:51:32.600
Fanny, Jeb, a street pusher.

1199
00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:39.040
And so we find out that Jeb has a nine-acre worm farm, which turns out worm means marijuana.

1200
00:51:39.320 --> 00:51:41.240
And then Aunt Shirley ends it with,

1201
00:51:41.480 --> 00:51:45.260
We can't just sit by and watch our family farm disappear, so here are my terMs.

1202
00:51:45.540 --> 00:51:49.400
Dwight, Fanny, and Jeb, if you come back home, I will leave you my farm.

1203
00:51:49.580 --> 00:51:51.140
So there, you have it.

1204
00:51:51.280 --> 00:51:56.660
So in this one video, we learn what the whole entire premise of the series is going to be.

1205
00:51:56.660 --> 00:52:03.820
Yes, we also learned earlier that Aunt Shirley's farm is, I guess, adjacent to Dwight's farm.

1206
00:52:04.100 --> 00:52:07.480
So they would have Dwight's farm and this farm, and they'd have all that land.

1207
00:52:07.840 --> 00:52:09.720
We now have two talking heads.

1208
00:52:10.100 --> 00:52:11.740
Jeb has a talking head and then Dwight.

1209
00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:14.180
There are two talking head locations on the farm.

1210
00:52:14.320 --> 00:52:17.900
You're either in the porch swing or you're in the rocking chair on the porch.

1211
00:52:17.900 --> 00:52:19.660
Oh, nice catch.

1212
00:52:20.440 --> 00:52:25.620
If you watch the talking heads in the rocking chair, Dwight has one and Zeke has one later,

1213
00:52:25.840 --> 00:52:28.320
you will see a blue Weber grill in the background.

1214
00:52:28.640 --> 00:52:28.880
Oh.

1215
00:52:29.380 --> 00:52:30.320
Isn't that so random?

1216
00:52:30.620 --> 00:52:33.060
Like a Weber grill, you know, with the lid that you lift up?

1217
00:52:33.240 --> 00:52:33.500
Yeah.

1218
00:52:33.860 --> 00:52:35.020
Yeah, just there.

1219
00:52:35.380 --> 00:52:38.060
Are you feeling like Aunt Shirley wouldn't have had a Weber grill?

1220
00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:39.480
I don't know.

1221
00:52:39.480 --> 00:52:42.340
It just seems like such random placement.

1222
00:52:42.920 --> 00:52:43.340
Hmm.

1223
00:52:43.580 --> 00:52:46.320
I wonder if there was like a little Weber grill deal or something.

1224
00:52:46.900 --> 00:52:47.860
It's not on a porch.

1225
00:52:47.860 --> 00:52:50.040
It's not anywhere where it looks like you would use it.

1226
00:52:50.160 --> 00:52:53.060
It's just tucked on the side of the wall of like a shed.

1227
00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:53.960
I don't know.

1228
00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:57.780
I just, every time I watched the talking heads, all I could think about was the Weber grill.

1229
00:52:58.060 --> 00:53:00.520
The Weber grill is really near and dear to my heart.

1230
00:53:00.680 --> 00:53:02.300
My dad grills on a Weber grill.

1231
00:53:02.440 --> 00:53:03.980
My dad had one for years.

1232
00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:07.000
Well, this is, I think now, clear why you spotted it.

1233
00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:07.840
Maybe so.

1234
00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:08.420
I missed it.

1235
00:53:08.880 --> 00:53:11.100
Well, Dwight is going to tell Fannie and Jeb, you know what?

1236
00:53:11.200 --> 00:53:12.360
We should do this.

1237
00:53:12.700 --> 00:53:13.420
We should.

1238
00:53:13.580 --> 00:53:15.240
And Fannie's like, I'm sorry, Dwight.

1239
00:53:15.240 --> 00:53:20.120
But, you know, a farm wife lacks the sophistication that she's used to.

1240
00:53:20.540 --> 00:53:20.880
Mm-hmm.

1241
00:53:21.300 --> 00:53:21.620
Yeah.

1242
00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:25.460
She says there's a sort of willing ignorance to the men.

1243
00:53:26.040 --> 00:53:27.840
And then she has a talking head.

1244
00:53:27.980 --> 00:53:29.060
She's on the porch swing.

1245
00:53:29.280 --> 00:53:33.200
It was very funny to me because she's like, I have written some poetry.

1246
00:53:33.380 --> 00:53:34.140
Thanks for asking.

1247
00:53:34.400 --> 00:53:34.680
Yeah.

1248
00:53:34.820 --> 00:53:36.960
I actually had a poem recently published.

1249
00:53:37.220 --> 00:53:38.140
Oh, do I have it?

1250
00:53:38.200 --> 00:53:38.640
Yes, I do.

1251
00:53:38.640 --> 00:53:39.360
Here it is.

1252
00:53:39.520 --> 00:53:45.540
It's from the HartfordWomensLitQuarterly.com, and it is titled A Willing Ignorance by Fannie

1253
00:53:45.540 --> 00:53:46.140
Schrute.

1254
00:53:47.020 --> 00:53:51.680
Lady, I paused on it, and I tried to, what do you call that, make it bigger?

1255
00:53:51.880 --> 00:53:52.220
Yes.

1256
00:53:52.560 --> 00:53:53.520
I took a picture.

1257
00:53:53.780 --> 00:53:54.120
Same.

1258
00:53:54.220 --> 00:53:54.760
I looked.

1259
00:53:54.940 --> 00:53:55.280
Same.

1260
00:53:55.380 --> 00:53:56.840
I really wanted to read her poem.

1261
00:53:57.020 --> 00:53:58.000
I really did, too.

1262
00:53:58.180 --> 00:54:03.100
And so I went to the writer's notes for this episode, and I found it.

1263
00:54:03.180 --> 00:54:03.980
You did not.

1264
00:54:04.160 --> 00:54:04.640
I did.

1265
00:54:05.120 --> 00:54:07.380
We're going to hear Fannie's poem right now.

1266
00:54:07.460 --> 00:54:08.360
We sure are.

1267
00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:09.540
Okay, I can't wait.

1268
00:54:09.700 --> 00:54:12.520
Here it is, A Willing Ignorance by Fannie Schrute.

1269
00:54:12.720 --> 00:54:17.320
The men I meet are nearly completely ignorant of all things worthwhile.

1270
00:54:17.940 --> 00:54:23.720
Whether current events or the classics, these gents think well-read is a lipstick shade for

1271
00:54:23.720 --> 00:54:24.740
a lady's smile.

1272
00:54:25.120 --> 00:54:25.520
Oh.

1273
00:54:25.760 --> 00:54:30.300
Their libraries consist of the Bible, of course, but it doesn't avert them from sin.

